The weight distribution is constant, \(W(M)=W_0\), between \(a=10^3\) and \(b=10^5\).

The number-average molecular weight is
\[
\bar M_{\mathrm n}
=\frac{\int_a^b W_0\,dM}{\int_a^b (W_0/M)\,dM}
=\frac{b-a}{\ln(b/a)}
\approx 2.15\times10^4.
\]

The weight-average molecular weight is
\[
\bar M_{\mathrm w}
=\frac{\int_a^b MW_0\,dM}{\int_a^b W_0\,dM}
=\frac{a+b}{2}
=5.05\times10^4.
\]

\[
\boxed{\left(2.15\times10^4,\;5.05\times10^4\right)}
\]

