Assuming three-point bending with a central load, use the support span \(L=5\) in., not the total sample length.

1. **Fracture force:** From \(\sigma_f=\dfrac{3FL}{2bh^2}\),
\[
F=\frac{2bh^2\sigma_f}{3L}
=\frac{2(0.5)(0.375)^2(45{,}000)}{3(5)}
=421.875\ \text{lb}.
\]

2. **Deflection at fracture:** The moment of inertia is
\[
I=\frac{bh^3}{12}
=\frac{(0.5)(0.375)^3}{12}
=0.00219727\ \text{in.}^4.
\]
With elastic deformation only,
\[
\delta=\frac{FL^3}{48EI}
=\frac{(421.875)(5)^3}{48(18\times10^6)(0.00219727)}
=0.02778\ \text{in.}
\]

\[
\boxed{(421.9,\;0.02778)}
\]

